commands.tekeco.morale.header=== %s morale ==
commands.tekeco.morale.noresidents=No villagers here yet.
commands.tekeco.morale.overview=Average happiness %s%s. Sulking: %s of %s
commands.tekeco.morale.overview.hover=Average of villagers in loaded chunks (0 to 100). Sulking villagers (under 20) walk slowly and barely work. The change is since the last payday.
commands.tekeco.morale.trend.down=, down %s %s
commands.tekeco.morale.trend.up=, up %s %s
commands.tekeco.morale.trend.same=, no change %s
commands.tekeco.morale.since.today=since this morning
commands.tekeco.morale.since.yesterday=since yesterday morning
commands.tekeco.morale.since.daysago=since %s days ago
commands.tekeco.morale.causes=Likely causes, biggest first (hover for details):
commands.tekeco.morale.causes.hover=Estimated from TekTopia's rules: how many villagers each cause affects, times its usual penalty. Everyday work slowly lowers everyone's happiness and isn't listed.
commands.tekeco.morale.nocauses=No obvious causes. Everyday work slowly lowers happiness; food, sleep, the Tavern and Bards bring it back.
commands.tekeco.morale.nocauses.hover=Checked: deaths, injuries, nitwits, beds, hunger, tools, leashes, wages, rent, the Tavern, crowding, school, and missing Tavern, Bard or Library.
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.deaths=%s villager deaths since yesterday
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.deaths.hover=Each death costs every villager with a bed 25 to 40 happiness. More Guards and a Cleric help keep villagers alive.
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.childdeaths=%s child deaths since yesterday
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.childdeaths.hover=A child's death costs every villager with a bed 50 to 65 happiness.
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.injuries=%s injuries today
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.injuries.hover=Villagers lose 8 happiness each time they're hurt (Guards and Clerics don't mind). More Guards and better lighting keep monsters away.
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.nitwits=%s nitwits
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.nitwits.hover=Nitwits lose 1 happiness every minute they're awake and get only a third of any boost. Give them a profession token from the Tradesman.
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.nobed=%s villagers without a bed
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.nobed.hover=Villagers without a bed can't sleep, so they miss the 10 to 30 happiness from waking up rested. Build more homes.
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.starving=%s starving
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.starving.hover=Starving villagers have nothing to eat, and eating is one of the main ways villagers get happier. Stock Storage with food.
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.hungry=%s hungry
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.hungry.hover=Hungry villagers are looking for food in Storage. Better and more varied food gives more happiness.
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.notool=%s workers without their tool
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.notool.hover=Farmers need a hoe, Lumberjacks and Butchers an axe, Miners a pickaxe, Guards a weapon. Each time they craft a replacement they lose 5 happiness. Keep tools in Storage.
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.leashed=%s leashed
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.leashed.hover=Leashed villagers slowly lose happiness, and break free when it reaches 0.
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.unpaid=%s unpaid at the last payday
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.unpaid.hover=The treasury couldn't pay their wage, so they lost happiness (unpaidPenalty, 10 by default). Deposit emeralds or have the Tradesman sell more.
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.cantafford=%s couldn't afford rent and food
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.cantafford.hover=At the last payday they couldn't pay rent and food, so they lost happiness (brokePenalty, 5 by default). Higher wages or lower rent help.
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.turnedaway=%s turned away from the Tavern
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.turnedaway.hover=They can't afford the Tavern tab, so they miss evenings at the Tavern until they have the money.
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.school=%s children at school
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.school.hover=Children at school sometimes sulk and lose 10 happiness. It passes, and school makes them better workers.
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.crowded=%s near %s is crowded or has a low ceiling
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.crowded.hover=Villagers lose up to 5 happiness each time they enter a building with fewer than 12 floor tiles each, or an average ceiling under 2.5 blocks. Make it bigger or raise the ceiling.
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.notavern=No Tavern
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.notavern.hover=Villagers relax at the Tavern in the evening; without one they miss that happiness. Build a Tavern.
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.nobard=No Bard
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.nobard.hover=Bards perform in the Tavern and around the village, cheering villagers up. Give a villager a Bard token.
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.nolibrary=No Library
commands.tekeco.morale.cause.nolibrary.hover=Villagers read at the Library's bookshelves for 2 happiness and some intelligence. Build a Library.
